            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Simple thing - I'd like my picker to try `git` tool first, and fallback to `rg`. Currently I don't think there is a way to achieve that, so I think it would be nice - either to be able to specify 'tool' as a table or to customize fallback order of tools\r\n>...\r\n> ... I'd like to default to rg when the CWD is not a git repo\r\n\r\nThere is a way by writing custom picker or overriding existing one. The `vim.fs.find` function can be used to determine whether a path is inside Git repo. So something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.pick').setup()\r\nMiniPick.registry.smart_files = function()\r\n  local tool = #vim.fs.find('.git', { upward = true }) > 0 and 'git' or 'rg'\r\n  return MiniPick.builtin.files({ tool = tool })\r\nend\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Simple thing - I'd like my picker to try <code class=\"notranslate\">git</code> tool first, and fallback to <code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code>. Currently I don't think there is a way to achieve that, so I think it would be nice - either to be able to specify 'tool' as a table or to customize fallback order of tools<br>\n...<br>\n... I'd like to default to rg when the CWD is not a git repo</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is a way by writing custom picker or overriding existing one. The <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.fs.find</code> function can be used to determine whether a path is inside Git repo. So something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.pick').setup()\nMiniPick.registry.smart_files = function()\n  local tool = #vim.fs.find('.git', { upward = true }) &gt; 0 and 'git' or 'rg'\n  return MiniPick.builtin.files({ tool = tool })\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">smart_files</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">tool</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">#</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fs</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">find</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>.git<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">upward</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> }) <span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>git<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>rg<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">builtin</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">files</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">tool</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">tool</span> })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "Simple thing - I'd like my picker to try git tool first, and fallback to rg. Currently I don't think there is a way to achieve that, so I think it would be nice - either to be able to specify 'tool' as a table or to customize fallback order of tools\n...\n... I'd like to default to rg when the CWD is not a git repo\n\nThere is a way by writing custom picker or overriding existing one. The vim.fs.find function can be used to determine whether a path is inside Git repo. So something like this:\nrequire('mini.pick').setup()\nMiniPick.registry.smart_files = function()\n  local tool = #vim.fs.find('.git', { upward = true }) > 0 and 'git' or 'rg'\n  return MiniPick.builtin.files({ tool = tool })\nend",
